%I A400570 #20 Nov 04 2026 21:29:21
%S A400570 1,1,6,18,62,166,509,1364,3903,10599,29423
%N A400570 Number of nonisomorphic rectangular dimonoids of order n.
%C A400570 A dimonoid is an algebraic structure (D,-|,|-) consisting of a set D equipped with two associative binary operations -| and |- satisfying the following axioms:
%C A400570   (x -| y) -| z = x -| (y |- z),
%C A400570   (x |- y) -| z = x |- (y -| z),
%C A400570   (x -| y) |- z = x |- (y |- z).
%C A400570 A dimonoid (D,-|,|-) is called rectangular if both (D,-|) and (D,|-) are rectangular semigroups in the sense that x -| y -| z = x -| z  and  x |- y |- z = x |- z for all x,y,z from D.
%H A400570 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.1080/00927872.2026.2712633">On dimonoids of small order</a>, Commun. Algebra, 1-15 (2026).
%H A400570 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.2607.17921">On dimonoids of small order</a>, arXiv:2607.17921 [math.GR], (2026).
%H A400570 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.23322631">Enumeration and lists of nonisomorphic rectangular dimonoids</a>, Zenodo, (2026).
%H A400570 Volodymyr M. Gavrylkiv, <a href="https://gist.github.com/vgavrylkiv/9a066fc0c6e0c1283baa231cb85c2895">C++ program for computing all pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular g-dimonoids and dimonoids</a>, GitHub Gist, (2026).
%e A400570 For n = 2, there are exactly 6 pairwise nonisomorphic rectangular dimonoids (D,-|,|-) on the set D={0,1}. Rows and columns are ordered as 0,1. The Cayley tables of all six dimonoids are listed below.
%e A400570 Dimonoid #1:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 0   0 0
%e A400570   0 0   0 0
%e A400570 Dimonoid #2:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 0   0 1
%e A400570   0 0   0 1
%e A400570 Dimonoid #3:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 0   0 0
%e A400570   1 1   0 0
%e A400570 Dimonoid #4:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 0   0 0
%e A400570   1 1   1 1
%e A400570 Dimonoid #5:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 0   0 1
%e A400570   1 1   0 1
%e A400570 Dimonoid #6:
%e A400570   -|:   |-:
%e A400570   0 1   0 1
%e A400570   0 1   0 1
%Y A400570 Cf. A027851, A400568, A400569, A390162, A398976, A401298.
